+  \item We derive the condition under which a conversion term raises aggregate biocapacity while $A_c$ falls, quantify sharp static identification intervals under independent observation packages, and compute signed integrated contribution budgets with refinement and closure checks. In a reduced fixed-demand comparison, the balance relation reaches the area floor without a fold or critical slowing; realized paths in the delayed model remain history-dependent. These are conditional model results, not general claims about observed ecosystems.
   \item We decompose NFA Edition 2026 account values for 1961--2023 and examine a separate cropland-area/yield proxy. The account series show a compositional change, not a census of physical ecological stocks.
