+\subsection{Integrated model contribution budgets}\label{sec:c13budget}
+
+A positive conversion component does not, by itself, establish the net rise in $B$. Extending \eqref{eq:identity} to active restoration and varying fast-land yield gives, almost everywhere along the projected trajectory,
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:c13fullbudget}
+\dot B=\underbrace{(b_f-u)u_c}_{\mathrm{conversion}}+
+\underbrace{b_f(\mu A_r-\eta_fA_f)}_{\mathrm{maintenance/retirement}}+
+\underbrace{uR_{rc}}_{\mathrm{restoration}}+
+\underbrace{b_{G,c}G_c'(q)A_c\dot q}_{\mathrm{quality\ readout}}+
+\underbrace{A_f\dot b_f}_{\mathrm{fast\ yield}},
+\end{equation}
+where $\dot b_f=e^{-\alpha D}\dot T_b-\alpha b_f\dot D$. Each displayed term has units gha\,yr$^{-1}$; its time integral has units gha. The last channel can therefore be split into technology and debt terms without changing the identity.
+
+We independently reconstructed the stated C12 numerical convention and integrated these five continuous-right-hand-side terms by trapezoidal quadrature on the saved state nodes. The integrals are compared with the independently evaluated endpoint change, not forced to sum to it. Seven nested steps from $0.05$ to $0.00078125$\,yr test numerical closure (SI~\S S10). No parameter, history, horizon, or delay is swept for a new experiment.
+
+Table~\ref{tab:c13budget} reports the frozen-demand run over $100$\,yr (F100) and the existing endogenous recovery case over $400$\,yr (R400). In F100, conversion adds about $0.547925$\,gha, offset mainly by $-0.311098$\,gha from maintenance/retirement; the endpoint rise is $0.231310$\,gha. In R400, the direct restoration contribution to $B$ is $0.016561$\,gha, while conversion contributes $0.513933$\,gha and maintenance/retirement $-0.218037$\,gha. These signed channels are bookkeeping along one coupled trajectory, not empirical causal effects or independent interventions. In particular, the negative quality-readout term comes from the specified non-monotone $G_c(q)$ while $q$ increases towards its imposed cap; it does not demonstrate physical quality loss.
